(skills/blender-asset-qa/scripts/qa_check.py and shared/_bpyx.py), Copyright (c) 2026 EL4CTEO,
licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE). Modified for cc-marketplace (2026-10-30):
- the _bpyx helpers it used (object resolution, mode switch, rounding) are inlined;
- bpy, bmesh and mathutils are imported only when present, so its pure parts load in plain Python;
- island grouping takes vertex and edge indices instead of a bmesh, so it is testable without Blender;
- it exits 0 on pass, 1 on errors (or warnings with --strict) and 2 when it cannot run. Upstream printed
  {"pass": false} and exited 0, which a CI step reads as success;
- output is a text summary or one --json object instead of the upstream @@JSON@@ marker line.

All other files are original to cc-marketplace. The skill and its references were written from primary
documentation and from probes of a Blender 5.2.3 LTS binary; facts first found in EL4CTEO/blender-skills,
ra100/blender-claude-plugin, MartinRapcan/blender-claude-skill and AiverReaver/blender-unreal-pipeline-skill
(all MIT) were re-verified before they were kept, and no upstream prose was copied.

